  "ref": "JOS.6.16",
  "review_notes": [
    "The supplied *when* is now its own `added` unit (rule 55); the הָיָה frame keeps only *it came to pass* (rules 21, 45), and the apodosis waw s014 stays `unrepresented` under rule 14, as in JOS.6.8.",
    "The competing reading, which the verse pass took, treats *when* as the frame's complementizer written in place of a *that*. It is rejected because rule 45 makes the frame's complementizer the word standing at the head of the apodosis, and because JOS.6.20 writes that same *when* for a כְּ morpheme while its *that* goes to the apodosis waw."
  ]
